{
  // Incremental JS→TS migration. `allowJs` + `checkJs: false` is what keeps
  // `tsc --noEmit` green while the tree is mixed: un-migrated .js files are
  // still pulled into the program transitively by imports, but never checked.
  //
  // `include` is scoped to the directories already converted and widens one
  // wave at a time — see docs/exec-plans/active/typescript-migration.md.
  //
  // EVERY WAVE MUST WIDEN `include` WITH THE FILES IT CONVERTS. `include` does
  // bound the program for any subtree nothing already in it imports, and the
  // failure is silent: a converted file left outside never enters the program,
  // so it goes unchecked while `tsc` stays green and the coverage claim reads
  // as true. Wave 3 hit exactly this — `src/lib/**` are leaves, so nothing in
  // the program reached `src/app/**`. Test dirs are the same trap: nothing
  // imports a test file at all.
  //
  // The mixed tree stays green because of `checkJs: false` — un-migrated .js
  // pulled in by imports is never checked — NOT because of `include`. So don't
  // widen it ahead of a wave either; that just costs the belt-and-braces.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    // vite/client supplies ImportMetaEnv (store/store.ts gates the
    // __hive_state e2e affordance on import.meta.env.VITE_WAILS_*).
    "types": ["vite/client"],
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": false,
    "noEmit": true,
    "strict": true,
    // The generated wailsjs/** and @xterm/* types are not ours to fix.
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    // React 19 automatic runtime — no `import React` needed in .tsx.
    "jsx": "react-jsx"
  },
  // test/unit is safe to include wholesale from wave 1: the un-converted
  // *.test.js files land in the program but `checkJs: false` skips them, so
  // each test starts being checked exactly when it's renamed to .ts.
  // test/e2e is wholesale as of wave 7b, which converted its 17 specs and the
  // xterm-reflow fixture. Nothing imports a spec or a harness (the Vite
  // substitution is invisible to tsc), so they are checked only by being named
  // here — the trap the comment above describes, and the reason the glob
  // widened in the same commit as the rename.
  // test/e2e-real joined them in wave 7c, the last of the migration. Its
  // globalSetup/globalTeardown stay .mjs and are skipped by `checkJs: false`.
  // src/main.tsx is named explicitly because nothing imports the entry
  // point — it is only reachable from index.html's <script src>, so it
  // drops out of the tsc program entirely if this list forgets it. It did,
  // once: the Phase 6 rename left "src/main.ts" here and the rewritten
  // composition root went unchecked. Keep the extension in sync.
  "include": [
    "src/lib/**/*",
    "src/app/**/*",
    "src/store/**/*",
    "src/components/**/*",
    "src/bridge.ts",
    "src/globals.d.ts",
    "src/main.tsx",
    "test/unit/**/*",
    "test/dom/**/*",
    "test/e2e/**/*",
    "test/e2e-real/**/*"
  ],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist", "wailsjs"]
}
